## 5. Connection String in Web.config

**Web.config exists in the `.csproj` but is NOT present on disk** (likely gitignored or excluded from the workspace). The connection string names referenced throughout the codebase are:

- **`DefaultConnectionString2`** -- primary connection string (used by `Core.DataFactory.CreateData()`)
- **`BConnectionString`** -- secondary connection string (used by `DCore.Data.CreateData()`)

Usage patterns found:
```csharp
// From BSims controls:
DCore.IData obj = DCore.Data.CreateData(ConfigurationManager.ConnectionStrings["BConnectionString"].ConnectionString, false);

// From Sims controls (commented out, now using SIM_Branch):
Core.IDB objIData = Core.DataFactory.CreateData(ConfigurationManager.ConnectionStrings["DefaultConnectionString2"].ConnectionString);
```

The actual connection string initialization happens in `SystemController.InitConnDB()` called from `BDS.Master.cs`:

```1:31:g:\0.CMS-MAIN-ALL-12\07-ha-tinh\his\BDS.Master.cs
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

using System.Web;
using System.Web.UI;
using System.Web.UI.WebControls;
using InformationWebObject;

namespace InformationWeb
{
    public partial class BDS : System.Web.UI.MasterPage
    {
        // Event nay se duoc chay truoc Page_Load cua cac control (nen dung dung hon la Page_Load)
        protected void Page_Init(object sender, EventArgs e)
        {
            SystemController.InitConnDB();
            if (!IsPostBack)
            {
                SystemController.TryLoginByToken(this); // tu dong login neu co token
            }
        }

        protected void Page_Load(object sender, EventArgs e)
        {

        }        
    }
}
```

