## 6. DAL / BLL Patterns

The project uses a **direct data object pattern** (not traditional 3-layer BLL/DAL). There are no separate BLL or DAL folders in this project.

### Primary Data Access Pattern: `SIM_Branch.GetDataTable()`

The main data access class is **`SimsObject.SIM_Branch`** (from external `SimsObject.dll`). It provides a generic stored-procedure calling method:

```csharp
SIM_Branch obj = new SIM_Branch();
DataTable dtb = obj.GetDataTable(
    "STORED_PROCEDURE_NAME",  // stored procedure name
    "@Param1", value1,        // param name, value pairs (variable arguments)
    "@Param2", value2,
    "@Param3", value3
);
```

This is the pattern used EVERYWHERE for data retrieval. Example from SubjectMarkDetail:

```69:76:g:\0.CMS-MAIN-ALL-12\07-ha-tinh\his\Controls\Learning\SubjectMarkDetail.ascx.cs
SIM_Branch obj = new SIM_Branch();
dtbData = obj.GetDataTable("SIM_SubjectMark_Search_SubjectMarkDetail", /* giong store tren window form tuong lau */
                                    "@ClassID", uClass.ClassID,
                                    "@DinhChi", bolDinhChi,
                                    "@YearID", uYearSemester.YearID,
                                    "@Semester", uYearSemester.Semester,
                                    "@IsFirst", chkIsFirst.Checked);
```

### Secondary Pattern: Direct Stored Procedure via `DCore.Data`

```csharp
DCore.IData obj = DCore.Data.CreateData(
    ConfigurationManager.ConnectionStrings["BConnectionString"].ConnectionString, false);
// Then call stored procedures on the obj
```

### Data Objects for CRUD

Individual objects like `SIM_SubjectMark`, `SIM_Class_Subject`, `SIM_YearDAO` exist in external DLLs for CRUD operations:

```csharp
// Reading a single object:
SIM_SubjectMark item = new SIM_SubjectMark();
item.Get();  or item.Parse(drw);

// Save:
item.Add() / item.Update()

// Transaction:
item.BeginTransaction();
// ... operations ...
item.CommitTransaction();
```

### Business Logic Service

```csharp
SimsService.SIM_SubjectMarkService.ToLearningLevel(drw, intRegulationID);
SimsService.SIM_SubjectMarkService.TotalRow(drw);
```

### Base Classes (from .csproj, files not on disk -- compiled into assembly)

- **`ControlBase`** -- base for all .ascx controls (used by SubjectMarkDetail)
- **`PageBase`** -- base for all .aspx pages (used by SubjectMarkDetail.aspx.cs)
- **`WebGlobal`** -- static helper class with `HasPermission()`, `InitDropDownList()`, `ToDouble()`, etc.
- **`MsgBox`** -- static class for showing messages (`MsgBox.ShowWarning()`, `MsgBox.ShowError()`, `MsgBox.Show()`)
- **`SystemController`** -- class with `InitConnDB()`, `TryLoginByToken()`

### User/Session Pattern

```csharp
DCore.SessionUser objUser = Session[DCore.Globals.USER] as DCore.SessionUser;
// Properties: objUser.UserName, objUser.StudentID, etc.
WebGlobal.StudentID  // static property for student ID
WebGlobal.HasPermission("PermissionKey")  // permission check
```

