## 7. Excel Export Functionality

Excel export uses **`Libs.CExcel.ExportTemplateExcel()`** from `Libs.dll`.

### Standard Pattern (from SubjectMarkDetail.ascx.cs):

```csharp
// 1. Prepare data
DataTable dtbExport = obj.GetDataTable("STORED_PROC", params...);

// 2. Path setup
string strPath = System.Web.HttpContext.Current.Server.MapPath("~");
string strFilePath = strPath + "Template\\Bang diem tong ket.xls";
string strFileNameSaveAs = "Bang diem tong ket - " + User.UserName + ".xls";
string strPathSaveAs = strPath + "Export\\" + strFileNameSaveAs;

// 3. Column mapping
Hashtable hstColumns = new Hashtable();
hstColumns.Add("StudentCode", "StudentCode");
hstColumns.Add("StudentFirstName", "StudentFirstName");
// ...

// 4. Template placeholder replacements
Hashtable hstReplaceValues = new Hashtable();
hstReplaceValues.Add("{Title}", strTitle);

// 5. Post-fill value replacements (e.g., -1 -> "M" for exempt)
Hashtable hstReplaceValuesAfterFill = new Hashtable();
hstReplaceValuesAfterFill.Add("-1", "M");

// 6. Export
if (Libs.CExcel.ExportTemplateExcel(dtbExport, strFilePath, "StudentCode", 
        hstColumns, hstReplaceValues, null, hstReplaceValuesAfterFill, strPathSaveAs))
{
    Response.Redirect("/Export/" + strFileNameSaveAs);
}
else
{
    MsgBox.ShowError("Viec xuat excel that bai");
}
```

**Both XML-based .xls template files** in the `Template/` folder are used.

